# Template for android/keystore.properties — a LOCAL, GITIGNORED file
# that must contain the real release-signing credentials once a real
# keystore exists. This example file is safe to commit (placeholders
# only); keystore.properties itself is NOT and must never be committed.
#
# Setup (see docs/android-release-signing.md for the full procedure):
#   1. Generate a real release keystore with `keytool` (not done by this
#      scaffold — no keystore is created automatically).
#   2. Copy this file to android/keystore.properties (same directory).
#   3. Fill in the four values below with your real keystore's details.
#
# storeFile: either an absolute path to the keystore file (recommended —
# keeps the real .jks/.keystore entirely outside this repo's directory
# tree), or a path relative to this android/ directory (also fine, and
# still gitignored via the *.jks/*.keystore rules in android/.gitignore,
# but a location outside the repo is safer against accidental staging).
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/your-release-key.jks
storePassword=REPLACE_WITH_REAL_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
keyAlias=REPLACE_WITH_REAL_KEY_ALIAS
keyPassword=REPLACE_WITH_REAL_KEY_PASSWORD
